me><surname>Archibald</surname><given-names>LK</given-names></name><name><surname>McDonald</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Addison</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>McKnight</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Byrne</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Dobbie</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nwanyanwu</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Kazembe</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Reller</surname><given-names>LB</given-names></name><name><surname>Jarvis</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of BACTEC MYCO/F LYTIC and WAMPOLE ISOLATOR 10 (lysis-centrifugation) systems for detection of bacteremia, mycobacteremia, and fungemia in a developing country</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>2994</fpage><lpage>2997</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10921966</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Collee</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Marmion</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name><name><surname>Irvine</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Fraser</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Simmons</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Mackie &#x00026; McCartney Practical Medical Microbiology</source><year>1996</year><edition>14</edition><publisher-name>New York , Churchill Livingstone</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NCCLS</collab></person-group><source>Performance Standards for Antimicrobial Disk Susceptibility Tests, Approved Standard M2-A7</source><year>1997</year><edition>7th</edition><publisher-name>Wayne, PA, USA , National Committee for Clinical Laboratory Standards</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blomberg</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Jureen</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Manji</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Tamim</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mwakagile</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Urassa</surname><given-names>WK</given-names></name><name><surname>Fataki</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Msangi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Tellevik</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Maselle</surname><given-names>SY</given-names></name><name><surname>Langeland</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High rate of fatal cases of pediatric septicemia caused by gram-negative bacteria with extended-spectrum beta-lactamases in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>745</fpage><lpage>749</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15695674</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.43.2.745-749.2005</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brakstad</surname><given-names>OG</given-names></name><name><surname>Maeland</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Tveten</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multiplex polymerase chain reaction for detection of genes for Staphylococcus aureus thermonuclease and methicillin resistance and correlation with oxacillin resistance [published erratum appears in APMIS 1994 Mar;102(3):241]</article-title><source>Apmis</source><year>1993</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>681</fpage><lpage>688</lpage><pub-id pub-id